    "b-30-integration-resolver-opening-2": {
      "id": "b-30-integration-resolver-opening-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The integration resolver resolves one queued integration conflict item — a genuine concurrency conflict where two workers started from the same base revision, the first patch landed, and the second no longer applies against the moved tree. It edits the cycle checkout directly, making the smallest conflict-resolution edits, and may return resolved, needs_rework, blocked, or rejected. The runner validates its melee_integration_resolver_result_v1 output (its schema is the group's only schema.json) and owns queue dispositions."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-30-integration-resolver-sources-3": {
      "id": "b-30-integration-resolver-sources-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Sources: removed. The integration-resolver agent was retired in the Knowledge System V2 refactor — an integration conflict is now a deterministic regression event ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "cause",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "merge_conflict",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ") plus a re-queue for the next epoch; no agent resolves integrations."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
